  "title": "P-ary m-sequence-based c-VEP dataset from Martínez-Cagigal et al. (2023)",
  "description": "A code-modulated visual evoked potential (c-VEP) brain-computer interface dataset employing p-ary m-sequences to enhance user comfort. The dataset comprises EEG recordings from 16 healthy subjects across 5 sessions with 8 runs per session, using an 11-class visual stimulus paradigm. This derivative dataset supports research into non-binary sequence designs for improving BCI usability and performance.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired at 256 Hz sampling rate using 16 channels in a standard 1005 montage with 50 Hz line frequency. Participants performed a c-VEP task with 11 visual stimulus classes presented in a trial interval of 0-1 seconds. Each session contained 8 runs (6 training, 2 testing) with visual stimuli annotated using HED 8.4.0 schema.",
  "license": "CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0",
